WEBVTT

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:08.920
Huh? Doesn't it seem more crowded than usual?

00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:12.010
I'm told today is the first day of a local celebration

00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:14.680
called the Sasahata Tanabata Festival.

00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:18.010
Well, here we are in Hatagaya,

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:22.520
but the MgRonald's we came to see is practically deserted.

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:24.520
This is no place for a proper fray!

00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:29.070
We need a bustling restaurant, or it'll suck when the mood sours...

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:31.570
Plus if the man we're after has the advantage,

00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:34.910
we might end up wrecking the work environment...

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:39.370
And the perfect place is standing right here! Sentucky!

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:41.410
We'll start with a council of war there!

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:44.830
Rika's totally enjoying this, isn't she...?

00:00:56.390 --> 00:01:00.680
<i>Right here, this moment,</i> <i>this is our starting point</i>

00:01:00.890 --> 00:01:06.690
<i>Let's picture what we might be able to do</i>

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:10.730
<i>Unbelievable things can happen sometimes</i>

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:16.450
<i>More... we can push past this</i>

00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:27.330
<i>Everything is born from zero;</i>
<i>I want to shine, flap my wings hard</i>

00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:31.800
<i>And fly to that sky</i>

00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:38.970
<i>Come on, let's go, with</i> <i>brilliant smiles on our faces!</i>

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:44.770
<i>Let's fly off to an unknown world right now</i>

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:49.360
<i>I decide, I'm the one who chooses my future</i>

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:51.730
<i>Let's follow our dreams</i>

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:53.280
<i>Sure, some days we'll cry</i>

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:59.660
<i>It's a precious wish, don't disappear</i>

00:01:59.870 --> 00:02:07.580
<i>I'm going after the future you,</i> <i>because I know I'll find you</i>

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:24.930
First, you'll have to tell me all about this "Maou" guy.

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:28.560
That might give us an idea for how to settle your battle.

00:02:28.770 --> 00:02:33.730
Given he's the Devil and I'm a hero, battle is all there's ever going to be.

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:39.410
But who knows how this girl's going to dodge Rika's misunderstanding...

00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:42.370
An iced coffee for me. How about you two?

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:46.620
I suppose I'll have a maple-biscuit-and-iced-tea set.

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:48.120
Milk in the tea, please.

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:49.500
Iced coffee.

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:52.500
I'll pay for all three of us.

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:53.380
Oh, that'll be all.

00:02:53.590 --> 00:02:55.170
Thank you, Miss.

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:59.550
May I present you with a Grand Opening coupon?

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:00.510
Thanks.

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:03.180
And now I shall lovingly prepare your order.

00:03:03.390 --> 00:03:08.270
Surely the food will appreciate being eaten by such lovely maidens.

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:10.270
Here's your change, Miss.

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:11.480
R-Right...

00:03:14.690 --> 00:03:15.820
Here you go.

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:21.450
It's a crime that I've kept a lady waiting.

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:24.990
Here is your order, Miss.

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:28.580
It's always men like that who turn out to suck at the "casual" thing

00:03:28.790 --> 00:03:30.580
and just end up a pain in the neck.

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:33.000
His sunglasses and cologne are in poor taste, too.

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:34.290
What are you talking about?

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:36.250
Nothing, never mind.

00:03:36.460 --> 00:03:37.760
Let's go.

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:43.220
Now, then! My first question is, how did things start?

00:03:43.430 --> 00:03:49.230
His name is Sadao Maou, right?
Both of you give it to me straight!

00:03:49.430 --> 00:03:52.100
To me, he's my neighbor at my new boarding house.

00:03:52.310 --> 00:03:54.480
I can say he's a good neighbor.

00:03:54.690 --> 00:03:55.820
This girl!

00:03:56.020 --> 00:04:00.780
I want you to take down King Satan with me, and then return to Ente Isla.

00:04:00.990 --> 00:04:06.660
After <i>that</i>, now he's a "good neighbor"?
She's cool as a cucumber, I'll give her that.

00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:07.950
And you, Emi?

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:11.040
Me, I'd happily kill him first chance I got.

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:12.830
Huh, conflicting opinions.

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:15.340
But since you always put up a front, Emi...

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:20.340
Look, Rika, I'm going to be frank: there's nothing between Maou and me.

00:04:20.550 --> 00:04:23.680
I have totally different reasons for not wanting him and Suzuno to be together,

00:04:23.890 --> 00:04:26.760
so we are <i>not</i> fighting over him!

00:04:26.970 --> 00:04:30.100
This is what I mean about you putting up a front.

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:33.980
Why are you so set on me and
Maou getting together, anyway?!

00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:35.650
Just thinking about it is infuriating!

00:04:35.860 --> 00:04:40.030
That man is savage and cunning and greedy and insensitive and poor and

00:04:40.230 --> 00:04:44.070
acts like you <i>owe</i> him for some random umbrella and has no common sense!

00:04:45.700 --> 00:04:47.910
I cannot let that remark pass, Yusa!

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:50.830
Ashiya?! What are you doing here?

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:57.290
Ashiya's taking a really long time...

00:04:58.130 --> 00:05:02.510
You want me to exhaustively consume the fried chicken of this "Sentucky"?

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:04.510
Well, it's not really about the eating part...

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:07.350
If you wanted me to exhaustively consume the offerings

00:05:07.550 --> 00:05:10.010
of the fried-food flash sale at the SIFE supermarket by the station

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:12.850
where I can get 100 grams for 88 yen, that would be one thing.

00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:16.100
But Sire, our army does not have the financial reserves

00:05:16.310 --> 00:05:19.570
to contribute to the sales of your present nemesis, SFC!

00:05:19.770 --> 00:05:21.900
Would you just listen to me?

00:05:22.110 --> 00:05:24.240
We're employing these methods because it <i>is</i> a potential nemesis.

00:05:24.450 --> 00:05:26.740
To win the battle, we must first know our enemy.

00:05:26.950 --> 00:05:29.490
You can't tell me that you, my top advisor, have forgotten that.

00:05:29.700 --> 00:05:30.910
Sire...

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:32.450
I'm not telling you to just eat.

00:05:32.660 --> 00:05:34.750
I want you to <i>eat, eat, eat</i> in an exhaustive investigation

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:38.290
of their strengths, weaknesses, and everything else!

00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:41.630
This is a necessary expense for my rise to power.

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:43.010
I beg your aid.

00:05:44.590 --> 00:05:49.350
If you feel that strongly,
Sire, I cannot refuse you.

00:05:49.550 --> 00:05:50.510
However!

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:53.850
I, Shiro Ashiya, will make my thoroughgoing investigation

00:05:54.060 --> 00:05:56.440
employing the minimum possible expenditure.

00:05:56.640 --> 00:05:57.270
Ashiya!

00:05:57.480 --> 00:05:59.230
Sire! Please leave this to me!

00:05:59.440 --> 00:06:00.110
Ashiya!

00:06:00.310 --> 00:06:00.940
--Ridiculous.
--Sire!

00:06:01.150 --> 00:06:02.530
Ashiya!

00:06:02.730 --> 00:06:06.360
I know I said "exhaustive," but he's taking too long!

00:06:06.570 --> 00:06:08.450
Mr. Maou?

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:10.280
Oh, Chi, what's up?

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:13.410
I got a bunch of chores done...

00:06:13.620 --> 00:06:17.540
Hmm? Oh. Right, let's see...

00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:23.170
Everyone's spirits are down...
Well, I guess that's to be expected.

00:06:23.380 --> 00:06:28.430
There's a huge crowd outside thanks to the Sasahata Tanabata Festival,

00:06:28.630 --> 00:06:33.680
and yet look at this state of affairs-- the complete opposite of our enemy SFC.

00:06:33.890 --> 00:06:37.310
What do I do? I can't just keep twiddling my thumbs!

00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:42.150
Um, maybe we should stand outside and invite people to eat here?

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:44.440
Soliciting customers... It's a possibility,

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:47.360
but it might be better to wait and devise countermeasures with Ashiya.

00:06:47.570 --> 00:06:49.570
And more importantly, the critical delivery isn't here yet,

00:06:49.780 --> 00:06:51.620
so how can we get the public's attention?

00:06:51.820 --> 00:06:56.410
Should I make a move now?
But--no, I mustn't act now!

00:06:56.620 --> 00:06:58.540
I can't predict this battle at all!

00:06:58.750 --> 00:07:01.540
Who knew fighting on the front lines of a major fast-food restaurant

00:07:01.750 --> 00:07:03.460
was so complex?!

00:07:03.670 --> 00:07:05.340
You okay, Maa?

00:07:05.550 --> 00:07:08.720
I know you're shift manager, but don't shoulder everything yourself.

00:07:08.930 --> 00:07:11.590
That's right! I'm commander of an army right now!

00:07:11.800 --> 00:07:14.850
If I show fear now, unrest will spread among my men!

00:07:15.060 --> 00:07:16.720
Now is not the time to act!

00:07:16.930 --> 00:07:19.520
Right now the tides are with them, that's all.

00:07:19.730 --> 00:07:23.940
But the tides are sure to turn!
We must wait for that moment!

00:07:24.150 --> 00:07:26.690
And to prepare for when it comes...

00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:30.700
Polish the windows!

00:07:30.910 --> 00:07:31.780
Roger!

00:07:31.990 --> 00:07:35.200
--All that thought and <i>that's</i> your conclusion?!
--Please... come quick!

00:07:35.410 --> 00:07:40.040
What are <i>you</i> doing here?
Or actually, where were you hiding?!

00:07:40.250 --> 00:07:44.630
I noticed you come in, but I wanted to avoid trouble.

00:07:44.840 --> 00:07:48.670
But I cannot allow you to abuse the master of my house in that manner.

00:07:48.880 --> 00:07:50.970
--It would stain my honor!
--Yeah, yeah.

00:07:51.180 --> 00:07:54.720
Oh, hey, this is a perfect opportunity.
Ashiya, give me a hand here!

00:07:54.930 --> 00:07:57.180
It's a matter of your dignity and Maou's.

00:07:57.390 --> 00:08:01.100
What? Why should I lend <i>you</i> a hand?

00:08:01.310 --> 00:08:04.440
You've got to be here to research this place, right?

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:06.360
I'll treat you to whatever you want.

00:08:06.570 --> 00:08:08.400
Well, if you insist.

00:08:08.610 --> 00:08:11.490
I didn't think you were <i>that</i> greedy.

00:08:11.700 --> 00:08:12.950
Don't get the wrong idea.

00:08:13.160 --> 00:08:16.700
Right now, I must prioritize the household budget above all else.

00:08:16.910 --> 00:08:20.710
For that, I shall bear any indignity;
I shall happily suffer any disgrace.

00:08:20.910 --> 00:08:22.330
You sound like a fool.

00:08:22.540 --> 00:08:25.840
At any rate, I was unable to research salads and desserts

00:08:26.040 --> 00:08:27.590
due to budget constraints.

00:08:27.800 --> 00:08:29.960
Later I shall order them.

00:08:30.170 --> 00:08:33.840
Um, I'm a little lost here... is he a friend?

00:08:34.050 --> 00:08:35.260
--Absolutely not!
--Absolutely not!

00:08:35.470 --> 00:08:37.140
I don't know who you are, Miss,

00:08:37.350 --> 00:08:41.390
but in terms of this group's relationships,
I am Miss Kamazuki's neighbor.

00:08:41.600 --> 00:08:43.390
My name is Shiro Ashiya.

00:08:43.600 --> 00:08:48.270
Nice to meet you.
I'm Rika Suzuki, a coworker of Emi's.

00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:52.450
If you're Suzuno's neighbor, does that mean you live with Mr. Maou?

00:08:52.650 --> 00:08:55.530
Yes. Do you know him, Miss?

00:08:55.740 --> 00:08:57.740
I'm asking because
I want to know all about him.

00:08:57.950 --> 00:08:59.620
Know... all about him?

00:08:59.830 --> 00:09:03.460
Eh, it's not the sort of thing you're worried about at all.

00:09:03.660 --> 00:09:09.590
Basically, this is about a man Emi doesn't want other girls getting close to.

00:09:09.800 --> 00:09:12.050
Yusa, what on Earth is she talking about?

00:09:12.260 --> 00:09:14.510
That's what I'd like to know, actually.

00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:18.890
A man Yusa doesn't want other girls getting close to, eh?

00:09:19.100 --> 00:09:21.470
And a matter of dignity?

00:09:21.680 --> 00:09:24.640
This is what the phrase "let the secret slip" means, Yusa.

00:09:24.850 --> 00:09:27.020
Well...

00:09:27.230 --> 00:09:30.520
I haven't told Miss Kamazuki this, either,

00:09:30.730 --> 00:09:33.740
but Maou and I once ran a company together.

00:09:33.950 --> 00:09:35.490
What?! A company?!

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:37.240
A-Ashiya?

00:09:37.450 --> 00:09:39.120
What is he talking about?

00:09:39.330 --> 00:09:43.450
Wait, you don't look much older than we are--how old <i>are</i> you?

00:09:43.660 --> 00:09:45.500
Our company mainly focused on

00:09:45.710 --> 00:09:49.170
real estate management and personnel placement.

00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:52.300
We also dabbled in construction and other industries occasionally.

00:09:52.500 --> 00:09:53.960
Yes, we were called...

00:09:54.170 --> 00:09:56.010
...the Maou Syndicate!

00:09:56.220 --> 00:09:57.510
Maou... Syndicate?

00:09:57.720 --> 00:09:59.550
"Personnel placement," my butt!

00:09:59.760 --> 00:10:01.470
And Yusa...

00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:03.810
...worked for a rival company!

00:10:04.020 --> 00:10:07.060
Emi, you worked in construction before?!

00:10:07.270 --> 00:10:09.520
More like, how old are you again?!

00:10:09.730 --> 00:10:11.360
Um, it's hard to explain...

00:10:11.570 --> 00:10:13.820
If I recall correctly, weren't you a temp at the time?

00:10:14.030 --> 00:10:14.780
A temp?!

00:10:14.990 --> 00:10:17.360
I see, so the hero is a temp...

00:10:17.570 --> 00:10:18.990
Don't take him seriously!

00:10:19.200 --> 00:10:21.030
Though we had our fingers in many pies, we were still small enough

00:10:21.240 --> 00:10:25.540
--that management had to command the teams on-site.
--Bring those materials over here.

00:10:25.750 --> 00:10:29.790
--But Yusa was both skilled and backed up by her company,
--Pleased to meet you. I'm Yusa.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:33.500
--and she frequently vied with us for our clients' jobs.
--...and so this structure...

00:10:33.710 --> 00:10:37.510
--We were all so young, and all with much the same level of business experience.
--I deeply apologize for the trouble!

00:10:37.720 --> 00:10:41.550
Japan was smack in the middle of the recession, and with a major firm taking jobs from us,

00:10:41.760 --> 00:10:45.730
our company run by young upstarts went down like a house of cards.

00:10:45.930 --> 00:10:47.640
--Mr. Company President!

00:10:45.930 --> 00:10:50.400
--And the final one to battle us for an order was Yusa.

00:10:47.640 --> 00:10:50.400
--Thank you so much, Mr. Company President!

00:10:50.600 --> 00:10:53.230
We lost, and the company went bankrupt.

00:10:53.440 --> 00:10:56.190
We drifted, eventually winding up in a Sasazuka apartment,

00:10:56.400 --> 00:10:59.610
until almost a year later, we saw Yusa again!

00:10:59.820 --> 00:11:00.870
Takoyaki...!

00:11:01.070 --> 00:11:06.750
I imagine Yusa had complex feelings about her fallen competitors.

00:11:06.950 --> 00:11:09.750
She still checks in on us every now and again.

00:11:09.960 --> 00:11:12.000
Oh, I <i>see.</i>

00:11:12.210 --> 00:11:12.840
However!

00:11:13.040 --> 00:11:16.670
Maou has not given up on his dream of starting a successful business!

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:19.760
Right now he is working intensely at MgRonald's

00:11:19.970 --> 00:11:22.090
to learn all about management from the ground up,

00:11:22.300 --> 00:11:25.930
and in just one year has been appointed shift manager.

00:11:26.140 --> 00:11:29.730
As for me, I now play housewife all day long...

00:11:29.940 --> 00:11:32.980
How far I have fallen.

00:11:33.190 --> 00:11:38.440
Nonetheless! We intend to start a business with our leader Maou again one day!

00:11:38.650 --> 00:11:41.240
I want to do everything
I can to support that dream!

00:11:41.450 --> 00:11:44.030
Still, entrepreneurship is a gamble.

00:11:44.240 --> 00:11:48.540
I can understand why Yusa didn't want
Miss Kamazuki to grow too close to us,

00:11:48.750 --> 00:11:52.830
out of fear that she'd get dragged into that gamble.

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:56.880
--I'm plenty dragged in already.
--And Maou is what you might call stubborn...

00:11:57.090 --> 00:12:00.970
He sees Yusa as an enemy, and hates her on a fundamental level.

00:12:01.180 --> 00:12:05.430
So I don't think the sort of thing you're imagining would ever happen, Miss Suzuki.

00:12:05.640 --> 00:12:09.730
Whoa, that sounds incredible... when you guys are about my age...

00:12:09.930 --> 00:12:12.600
Now I'm embarrassed that I had such a wild idea and blew it out of proportion

00:12:12.810 --> 00:12:13.900
and butted into things.

00:12:14.110 --> 00:12:16.690
And Emi, you should have told me!

00:12:16.900 --> 00:12:19.320
You wouldn't have listened, would you?

00:12:19.530 --> 00:12:23.410
My family runs a small factory, and when times really got rough,

00:12:23.610 --> 00:12:25.990
we pulled through it by all working together.

00:12:26.200 --> 00:12:27.830
You said you'd "fallen," but your Mr. Maou

00:12:28.040 --> 00:12:31.960
eats the meals you've made, sleeps on the futon you've aired out,

00:12:32.160 --> 00:12:35.420
and wears the underwear you've washed, right?

00:12:35.630 --> 00:12:36.290
Yes...

00:12:36.500 --> 00:12:41.170
Then you're everyone's firm foundation, so I think you should be prouder of yourself.

00:12:41.380 --> 00:12:47.180
Since you're supportive of each other like that, I know things will go well!

00:12:47.390 --> 00:12:50.850
You're the first person who's ever said that to me.

00:12:51.060 --> 00:12:54.400
Thank you for encouraging me--
I feel a bit stronger for it.

00:12:57.190 --> 00:12:59.020
--Rika?
--Huh?! What?!

00:12:59.230 --> 00:13:02.240
Uh, I'm kind of asking <i>you</i> that.
What's gotten into you?

00:13:02.450 --> 00:13:05.280
It's nothing, it's nothing, it's nothing, it's nothing!

00:13:05.490 --> 00:13:06.660
She said that four times.

00:13:06.870 --> 00:13:09.910
But wow, everybody's got a past, huh?

00:13:10.120 --> 00:13:12.710
Anyway, this clears up the misunderstanding, right?

00:13:12.910 --> 00:13:13.660
Let's go home--

00:13:13.870 --> 00:13:16.420
Now I'm personally interested in checking out this "Maou" guy!

00:13:16.630 --> 00:13:17.000
Huh?!

00:13:17.210 --> 00:13:22.050
For one thing, if he's so gifted, I should invest in making the connection now!

00:13:22.260 --> 00:13:23.340
Hold it, what are you talking about?

00:13:23.550 --> 00:13:26.090
Mr. Ashiya, you need to report to him about the enemy, right?

00:13:26.300 --> 00:13:28.550
--So why don't we all go together?
--Whoa, Rika!

00:13:28.760 --> 00:13:30.720
You're coming too, of course?

00:13:30.930 --> 00:13:32.850
Now get me one of those maple biscuits

00:13:33.060 --> 00:13:36.310
and a salad with Thousand
Island dressing, takeout.

00:13:36.520 --> 00:13:39.020
--Hey-- Wait--
--Miss Kamazuki, I must thank you for your constant help.

00:13:39.230 --> 00:13:41.320
Allow me to treat you.

00:13:43.070 --> 00:13:44.990
Why did things turn out like this?

00:13:52.540 --> 00:13:56.210
The situation is getting worse and worse.

00:13:56.420 --> 00:13:57.750
Oh my, Miss.

00:13:57.960 --> 00:14:02.920
If you allow things to trouble you so, you won't be able to enjoy your food.

00:14:03.130 --> 00:14:04.670
Uh, thanks, I guess.

00:14:04.880 --> 00:14:05.970
No matter how much one worries,

00:14:06.180 --> 00:14:09.680
over time things change whether we like it or not.

00:14:09.890 --> 00:14:14.810
I hope you won't regret it when the situation becomes totally out of your control.

00:14:15.020 --> 00:14:19.270
This is the first time I've been given advice on life by an SFC employee.

00:14:19.480 --> 00:14:21.860
Oh, I'm sorry for being presumptuous.

00:14:22.070 --> 00:14:24.110
But please let me tell you just one thing.

00:14:24.320 --> 00:14:27.610
Men take advantage of women when they're vulnerable.

00:14:27.820 --> 00:14:30.030
Please be on your guard at all times.

00:14:30.240 --> 00:14:31.620
What do you mean by that?

00:14:31.830 --> 00:14:34.450
Well, nothing really.

00:14:34.660 --> 00:14:38.920
Thank you very much. Please come see us again.

00:14:44.050 --> 00:14:46.300
They're giving out Grand Opening coupons, eh?

00:14:46.510 --> 00:14:48.630
Furthermore, I tried their food, too.

00:14:48.840 --> 00:14:50.970
Their trademark product, fried chicken, is amazing!

00:14:51.180 --> 00:14:54.390
Depending on the part of the chicken, you can even eat the bones!

00:14:54.600 --> 00:14:56.140
Even bones?!

00:14:56.350 --> 00:14:57.690
Wait. People don't normally eat bones.

00:14:57.890 --> 00:15:01.650
And that's not all.
They evidently serve organic coffee.

00:15:01.860 --> 00:15:03.860
Coffee made from ogres?!

00:15:04.070 --> 00:15:06.400
"Organic." It means "grown with natural pesticides."

00:15:06.610 --> 00:15:08.900
Naturally pestilent ogres, eh?

00:15:09.110 --> 00:15:12.530
But besides those things, I don't think there's an extreme difference.

00:15:12.740 --> 00:15:14.830
Their customer service was quite normal, too.

00:15:15.040 --> 00:15:19.000
The only reason I can think of at this point is that passersby are just drawn to new things.

00:15:19.210 --> 00:15:20.370
I see.

00:15:21.290 --> 00:15:24.210
In any case, we'll at least try putting up a fight.

00:15:24.420 --> 00:15:25.500
Thanks for your help.

00:15:25.710 --> 00:15:27.380
I hardly deserve those words.

00:15:27.590 --> 00:15:33.180
Although it's not much,
I'll contribute to your sales, Sire.

00:15:33.390 --> 00:15:38.850
Two Big Mag burger sets with large drinks and fries, please.

00:15:39.060 --> 00:15:42.480
Urushihara will probably complain, but this'll be our dinner tonight.

00:15:42.690 --> 00:15:45.860
If he complains about the food, give him a good beating. I'll give you permission.

00:15:46.070 --> 00:15:48.240
--As you wish, Sire.
--Ah-choo!

00:15:48.440 --> 00:15:51.740
In addition... please expect great things from those girls.

00:15:51.950 --> 00:15:54.330
Okay... though I don't know what you mean.

00:15:54.530 --> 00:15:57.950
Well then, I pray for your success in battle.

00:15:59.200 --> 00:16:03.710
Wow, they seem really tight.
On top of that, he acts totally professional.

00:16:03.920 --> 00:16:05.880
You're surrounded by capable people, Emi.

00:16:06.090 --> 00:16:08.760
Oh, can I count myself among them?

00:16:08.960 --> 00:16:10.420
Knock yourself out.

00:16:10.630 --> 00:16:13.220
Their chairs are harder than the ones at SFC...

00:16:13.430 --> 00:16:16.720
Excuse me, M-i-s-s-e-s...

00:16:16.930 --> 00:16:17.850
What?

00:16:18.060 --> 00:16:21.980
Could you sit down after you've placed your order?

00:16:22.190 --> 00:16:24.940
Then bring me a small iced coffee.

00:16:25.150 --> 00:16:28.530
Our restaurant is self-service. We'd like our customers to order at the register.

00:16:28.730 --> 00:16:32.780
Fine, I'll order an apple pie too, so show some gratitude and bring it to the table.

00:16:32.990 --> 00:16:35.240
--Miss--
--You're <i>the</i> Mr. Maou, aren't you?

00:16:35.450 --> 00:16:38.160
You somehow aren't as charismatic as I thought you'd be.

00:16:38.370 --> 00:16:40.790
Your restaurant is empty when you're in charge, too.

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:44.500
What're you saying out of nowhere?
Who do you think you are?!

00:16:44.710 --> 00:16:47.380
Hey, that's not very polite!

00:16:47.590 --> 00:16:50.550
You want me to send a letter to your headquarters telling them that you've got an attitude?

00:16:50.760 --> 00:16:55.260
Shut up! Restaurants have rules that even customers need to follow.

00:16:55.470 --> 00:16:56.760
Besides, who the heck are you?!

00:16:56.970 --> 00:17:00.020
I'm Rika Suzuki. I'm Emi's coworker.

00:17:00.220 --> 00:17:04.480
Mr. Sadao Maou. These two and
Mr. Ashiya told me about you.

00:17:04.690 --> 00:17:07.610
Ashiya did? When? What did he tell you?

00:17:07.820 --> 00:17:09.230
Ah-choo!

00:17:09.440 --> 00:17:13.450
Well, Mr. Ashiya and Emi's opinions of you were totally one-sided,

00:17:13.650 --> 00:17:16.280
so I came to check you out myself.

00:17:16.490 --> 00:17:21.700
I don't get what you're saying, but are you one of those busybody types?

00:17:21.910 --> 00:17:24.670
Seriously, first there's no customers and then Emi shows up...

00:17:24.870 --> 00:17:27.630
You shouldn't talk like that, Mr. Maou!

00:17:27.840 --> 00:17:30.670
Miss Yusa is also a valuable customer.

00:17:30.880 --> 00:17:34.260
Here you go! Iced coffee and an apple pie fresh from the oven!

00:17:34.470 --> 00:17:37.930
Sorry, Chiho. I just got carried away because of Maou...

00:17:38.140 --> 00:17:40.140
Don't worry about it. I know.

00:17:40.350 --> 00:17:42.430
Good Chiho, you seem to be working hard.

00:17:42.640 --> 00:17:44.140
Hi, Miss Suzuno!

00:17:44.350 --> 00:17:46.850
Are you Miss Yusa's friend?

00:17:47.060 --> 00:17:49.730
That's right. I'm Emi's coworker. I'm Rika Suzuki.

00:17:49.940 --> 00:17:51.980
I'm Chiho Sasaki.

00:17:52.190 --> 00:17:54.820
Miss Yusa has been very nice to me.

00:17:55.030 --> 00:17:55.860
How cute...

00:17:56.070 --> 00:17:56.740
Excuse me?

00:17:56.950 --> 00:17:59.740
How cute! What's with this girl?! She's so cute!

00:17:59.950 --> 00:18:01.830
Hey, what're you doing?!

00:18:02.040 --> 00:18:04.620
Isn't it unfair how many gifted people you have around you, Emi?!

00:18:04.830 --> 00:18:07.250
She's polite and has good work ethics.

00:18:07.460 --> 00:18:10.170
On top of that, she's cute!
That's cheating! Cheating I tell you!

00:18:10.380 --> 00:18:13.010
Hey, what are you, a drunk old man? Stop it, Rika!

00:18:13.210 --> 00:18:14.260
Okay, okay.

00:18:14.470 --> 00:18:17.630
Sorry, Chiho. I just got so excited.

00:18:17.840 --> 00:18:21.850
O-Okay, though I don't know what this is about...

00:18:22.060 --> 00:18:24.270
So what're you gonna do now?

00:18:24.480 --> 00:18:24.890
Huh?

00:18:25.100 --> 00:18:28.600
You told Mr. Ashiya that you'd try putting up a fight or something.

00:18:28.810 --> 00:18:32.980
This is a good chance, so I'll just say it straight... I want to see how you work.

00:18:33.190 --> 00:18:34.900
What the heck is your deal?

00:18:35.110 --> 00:18:37.530
Mr. Ashiya... Chiho...

00:18:37.740 --> 00:18:40.030
There are many gifted people around Emi.

00:18:40.240 --> 00:18:44.370
So I'm guessing that you aren't the idiot that you appear to be.

00:18:44.580 --> 00:18:48.040
In short, you're trying to say that I look like an idiot?

00:18:48.250 --> 00:18:50.580
It might be more than just looks.

00:18:51.840 --> 00:18:53.250
Fine!

00:18:53.460 --> 00:18:55.550
The hell with SFC's coupons!

00:18:55.760 --> 00:18:57.420
We'll compete by using flyers!

00:18:57.630 --> 00:18:59.300
How about some MgRonald's burgers?!

00:18:59.510 --> 00:19:01.760
Please stop by!

00:19:03.430 --> 00:19:05.470
--It's no use!
--What?!

00:19:05.680 --> 00:19:09.390
Then, we'll advertise that our products don't have bones and are easy to eat!

00:19:09.600 --> 00:19:14.230
How about a Big Mag burger?!
They don't have bones and are easy to eat!

00:19:14.440 --> 00:19:17.490
Isn't it just natural that burgers don't have bones?

00:19:17.690 --> 00:19:18.990
You say some silly stuff!

00:19:19.200 --> 00:19:20.530
You're cute!

00:19:20.740 --> 00:19:21.570
It's no use.

00:19:21.780 --> 00:19:23.160
Yeah, I guess...

00:19:24.160 --> 00:19:26.750
Kawa-cchi! Now that it's come to this, isn't it time for us to begin

00:19:26.950 --> 00:19:29.290
Operation Let People Use the Restroom
Even if They Don't Buy Anything?!

00:19:29.500 --> 00:19:31.380
What's the point of that?!

00:19:33.210 --> 00:19:34.590
How pathetic...

00:19:36.460 --> 00:19:38.090
Is Maou in?

00:19:38.300 --> 00:19:40.800
Mr. Nabe! I've been waiting for you!

00:19:41.010 --> 00:19:45.680
It's a request from you, of course
I'd come! Sorry I'm a little late.

00:19:45.890 --> 00:19:48.100
No problem! You're a life-saver!

00:19:48.310 --> 00:19:50.770
It'll be my treat, so please have something!

00:19:50.980 --> 00:19:52.690
Now that I've delivered what you asked for, I'll go home.

00:19:52.900 --> 00:19:56.440
My wife's making dinner for me, so...
Thanks for your offer, though.

00:19:56.650 --> 00:20:00.450
I'll see you on the next cleaning day.
Say hello to Miss Kisaki.

00:20:04.450 --> 00:20:06.830
Amazing! He gave us really nice ones!

00:20:07.040 --> 00:20:09.710
Let's hurry up and decorate before the dinner rush starts!

00:20:09.910 --> 00:20:11.330
Yeah, let's do it!

00:20:11.540 --> 00:20:13.290
Maa, here you go!

00:20:13.500 --> 00:20:15.130
Do you think we have enough ornaments?

00:20:15.340 --> 00:20:17.000
Okay, let's use the flyers.

00:20:18.170 --> 00:20:20.840
Is it okay to use them to make ornaments?

00:20:21.050 --> 00:20:23.840
I'm the current shift manager.
I'll give you permission!

00:20:24.050 --> 00:20:25.220
What's going on?

00:20:25.430 --> 00:20:28.560
The Sasahata Tanabata Festival gave Mr. Maou the idea.

00:20:28.770 --> 00:20:31.690
He thought we'd have customers write their wishes on strips of paper

00:20:31.890 --> 00:20:35.150
and decorate the trees using them.

00:20:35.360 --> 00:20:40.280
He asked the manager to get permission from our regional office

00:20:40.490 --> 00:20:44.780
to give a complimentary small drink to the customers who participated.

00:20:45.660 --> 00:20:49.580
He then asked that old man who came by earlier, Mr. Watanabe, for the trees.

00:20:49.790 --> 00:20:53.250
Mr. Maou got to know him while volunteering for neighborhood cleanup,

00:20:53.460 --> 00:20:55.790
and learned that he grows bamboo trees in his yard.

00:20:56.000 --> 00:20:59.250
Maou... volunteers for neighborhood cleanup...?

00:20:59.460 --> 00:21:02.840
Of course, we don't know if this will directly affect our sales,

00:21:03.050 --> 00:21:06.010
but the mood in the restaurant has changed a bit, right?

00:21:06.220 --> 00:21:08.060
--All right!
--Whoa!

00:21:09.060 --> 00:21:11.020
Good!

00:21:11.220 --> 00:21:13.230
He <i>is</i> pretty good.

00:21:14.850 --> 00:21:17.810
I'll admit that he's a hard worker.

00:21:18.020 --> 00:21:19.190
Oh?

00:21:20.190 --> 00:21:20.900
How pretty!

00:21:21.110 --> 00:21:23.650
Is this the MgRonald's with that cute girl who says silly things?

00:21:23.860 --> 00:21:25.700
I saw her pic in a tweet!

00:21:25.910 --> 00:21:26.570
What is it?!

00:21:26.780 --> 00:21:29.280
Mom, I wanna write my wish and decorate it!

00:21:31.580 --> 00:21:33.410
What?! Seriously?!

00:21:33.620 --> 00:21:36.790
They just put bamboo trees out and now this? What kind of feng shui is it?

00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:39.500
I can't believe it!

00:21:39.710 --> 00:21:42.420
All right, guys! Take up battle positions!

00:21:42.630 --> 00:21:43.670
It's time for war!

00:21:43.880 --> 00:21:45.680
Yeah!

00:21:45.880 --> 00:21:47.890
Welcome! Welcome!

00:21:48.100 --> 00:21:51.930
Once you've decided on your order, please get in line!

00:21:54.100 --> 00:21:58.020
Welcome! The seats over there are not taken.

00:21:58.230 --> 00:22:00.770
Okay. I'll show you the way.

00:22:18.130 --> 00:22:23.510
<i>Where will morning start from, in this quiet sky?</i>

00:22:23.710 --> 00:22:29.140
<i>Fingertips twining in a pinky</i> <i>swear I pretended not to see</i>

00:22:29.340 --> 00:22:39.340
<i>If the moon's been laughed at,</i> <i>she'll sink away toward yesterday</i>

00:22:40.020 --> 00:22:45.280
<i>Liar, coward--if I'm all these things at once</i>

00:22:45.490 --> 00:22:50.990
<i>Then I only blossomed in dreams</i>

00:22:51.200 --> 00:22:56.540
<i>I hid in the moon's shadow,</i> <i>but the truth is, I was crying</i>

00:22:56.750 --> 00:23:02.250
<i>The tears won't flow anymore--</i> <i>did they all dry up?</i>

00:23:02.460 --> 00:23:08.800
<i>If I could forgive everything,</i> <i>maybe they'd flow again</i>

00:23:09.010 --> 00:23:16.350
<i>But these are all things I want to protect</i>
